      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y + x^{2} y=x y^{2}\\,,\\ y\\ne 0\\,.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y + x^{2} y&=x y^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y + x^{2} y - x y^{2}&=0 \\\\ y (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + x^{2} - x y)&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + x^{2} - x y&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- x)}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{- x^{2}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- x)}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{- x^{2}}_{Q(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=- x$ and $Q(x)=- x^{2}.$",
