    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a9d344a5-fbee-53c2-9030-d94f45ef925c",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}}{x^{2}}=\\frac{x + 2 y}{x}\\,,\\ x\\ne 0\\,.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}}{x^{2}}&=\\frac{x + 2 y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}&=x^{2} \\frac{x + 2 y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}&=x (x + 2 y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}&=x^{2} + 2 x y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- 2 x)}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{x^{2}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- 2 x)}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{x^{2}}_{Q(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=- 2 x$ and $Q(x)=x^{2}.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "6a49c9af-10ce-5f5e-bf9e-a6160e98b18b",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
