      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n- \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y e^{- x} + 7 y^{2}=y\\,,\\ y\\ne 0\\,.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y e^{- x} + 7 y^{2}&=y \\\\ - \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y e^{- x} + 7 y^{2} - y&=0 \\\\ - y (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{- x} - 7 y + 1)&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{- x} - 7 y + 1&=0 \\\\ (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{- x} - 7 y + 1) e^{x}&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} - 7 y e^{x} + e^{x}&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- 7 e^{x})}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{- e^{x}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- 7 e^{x})}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{- e^{x}}_{Q(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=- 7 e^{x}$ and $Q(x)=- e^{x}.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
